  "verified_invariants": [
    "Legacy scope, typed eight-byte size markers and first compressed frames remain valid; cache initialization rejects unrelated directories and recognized repository storage",
    "Persistent access order and shared configured byte/typed-entry limits are enforced across opens and independent concurrent instances",
    "Tree/Blob registrations share physical payload bytes; marker eviction frees payload only after the final registration is removed",
    "Oversized individual frames are returned uncached and do not evict existing objects; exact first zstd representation is preserved",
    "Snapshot validation and actual-size capacity preflight precede admission; every validated manifest key remains pinned throughout publication",
    "Concurrent exports/readers exclude eviction while reading; in-memory frames already returned remain valid after deletion",
    "Dirty intent survives interrupted file mutation; actual SIGSTOP observes committed-catalog/file disagreement before SIGKILL; recovery respects limits and integrity_check passes",
    "Synthetic publication/eviction interruption cases, orphan/staging cleanup, signed integer boundary and symlink rejection are covered",
    "Real Unix-socket daemon enforces one-entry capacity, refetches evicted data through its configured cache hop, serves a warm hit after SIGKILL/restart, and skips oversized admissions",
    "Real daemon retains one managed periodic snapshot after multiple cycles and preserves an operator archive; diagnostics avoid disk lock waits"
  ],
